ing, or expert ratings are available. No general-election polls of the race have been published, leaving the state's underlying partisan fundamentals as the main guide.\n\nHeadlines from 2026 hint at Democratic energy: August midterm results were described as real trouble for Florida Republicans, and analysts flagged the state as a 2028 proving ground for the party. That evidence is indirect, however, tied to down-ballot races rather than the presidential contest. The rating stays in Lean Republican territory, with wide uncertainty reflecting the absence of direct polling.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.2832, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.3401, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.352, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.3574, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.3329, "margin": -4.5}]}